# Project Principles

## Code Style

- Do not add comments to code
- Do not create index.ts barrel files - import directly from actual source files
- Keep libraries to a minimum

## Project Structure

- Use feature-based folder structure
- Each feature contains `hooks/` and `components/` folders
- Each feature has a root component (e.g., `CounterPage.tsx` for the counter feature)

## Separation of Concerns

- Hooks contain all logic (state, effects, API calls, navigation)
- Components handle only UI rendering
- Components reference logic from hooks

## Styling

- Keep inline styling in components minimal - only use paddings, margins, and layout
- Colors, shadows, typography, and theming must come from the design system tokens
- Use CSS variables from `index.css` for design tokens (e.g., `var(--spacing-md)`, `var(--text-lg)`)

## Git

- When adding new project-related files, run `git add` on them

